-- title:
--   Base change of the level-N modular function field to ℚ̄
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a natural number, assumed nonzero. Inside the field $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ of formal Laurent series over an algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$, two intermediate fields over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ are compared. The first is `modularFunctionFieldBar N`, by definition `laurentBaseChange` of `modularFunctionFieldFull N` along $\mathbb{Q} \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$: that is, the subfield generated over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ by the image, under the coefficientwise embedding `coeffEmb` of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\mathbb{Q})$ into $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$, of the underlying set of the intermediate field $\mathbb{Q}(\,\mathrm{divisorExpansions}\ N\,)$ of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\mathbb{Q})$ obtained by adjoining to $\mathbb{Q}$ the set `divisorExpansions N` of Laurent series. The second is `modularFunctionFieldC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) N`, the subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ by the two elements $\mathrm{jqModC}$, namely $q^{-1}$ (the Hahn series `single (-1) 1`) times the image of the integral power series `jNum` under the coefficient map $\mathbb{Z} \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and its substitution $q \mapsto q^{N}$ under `qExpand`, written $\mathrm{jqNModC}$. The assertion is that these two intermediate fields are equal.
--
--   This identifies the constant-field extension to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the level-$N$ modular function field with the field generated by the $q$-expansions of $j(q)$ and $j(q^{N})$ alone, for every nonzero $N$ and with no primality hypothesis. It is the form of the function field used in the subsequent place, divisor and genus arguments at composite level, which are carried out over an algebraically closed field of constants.
